From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 697/699] clk: mediatek: mt6797: power VDECSYS through runtime
 PM

The VDECSYS gate registers live inside the VDEC power domain. With the
domain described, let the clock core power it for register access, so
reading the gate state with the domain off cannot touch an unpowered
block.
---
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-vdec.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-vdec.c b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-vdec.c
index 80bbbb0c4..0247bb7e3 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-vdec.c
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@ static const struct mtk_clk_desc vdec_desc = {
 	.num_clk_ids = CLK_VDEC_NR,
 	.clks = vdec_clks,
 	.num_clks = ARRAY_SIZE(vdec_clks),
+	.need_runtime_pm = true,
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id of_match_clk_mt6797_vdec[] = {
